WEBVTT

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.380
It happened last summer...

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.500
At the Senior Little League nationals...

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.400
<b>The All-Japan Senior Little League Baseball Championship</b>

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.610
<b>The All-Japan Senior Little League Baseball Championship</b>

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.010
Strike three!

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.200
Kuramoto Chuo

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.200
Fujiura

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.190
We've got this in the bag.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:19.950
Yeah!

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.110
Safe!

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.950
We're just getting started!

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.280
No way. It's too late.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:05.620
Safe!

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.010
Sorry.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.050
Don't sweat it.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:13.510
Let's not give up
any more runs this inning!

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.970
Not like we can catch up, anyway.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.470
Isn't this fun?

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.470
H-How is this fun?

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.930
I mean, we all get to play 
together in this huge stadium!

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.390
We still have two innings left.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.310
Let's just enjoy every last second!

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.420
You really don't know when 
to give up, do you, Arihara?

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.530
Damn... We can't lose heart now!

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.170
You've got this! Give it all you've got!

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.570
You can hit it!

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:51.130
C'mon, get us a hit!

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.080
Yes!

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.450
Keep going! Keep going!

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.850
What the heck were you doing?

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:18.710
Huh?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.080
Nice pitching!

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.090
Thanks!

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:40.800
We can do this!

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.760
Swing for the fences!

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.640
Let's see a home run!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.930
We're just getting started!

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.880
<i>What's her deal?</i>

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.490
Timeout!

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.500
That ball was yours!

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.450
Huh?!

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.770
You've been missing everything today!

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.180
That's enough!

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.210
We're not just playing around here!

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.500
<i>I can't let it end here.</i>

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.480
<i>I have to win this tournament 
and keep moving forward.</i>

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.980
Arihara! Knock it out of the park!

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:38.320
<i>Shut up.</i>

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.870
It's all on you!

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.000
<i>Be quiet!</i>

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.700
I can't believe you clawed it back
 and won with a walk-off grand slam!

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.730
Arihara's got the right stuff!

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.110
That game was incredible!

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:19.730
Tsubasa was the only one
communicating at first,

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.470
but eventually, the whole
team found its voice.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.090
Yeah.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.550
And, riding that wave, the team
went on to win the tournament.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:32.410
Miss Arihara, how did it feel when 
your team won the championship?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.380
I thought, "My baseball days are over."

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.940
<b>Though We May Stand at a Crossroads</b>

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.900
For a good six months after that summer,
I didn't play any baseball at all.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:29.990
If it wasn't for Tomocchi,

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.700
I probably would've quit for good.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.920
Arihara

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.020
Tsubasa? I'm coming in.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.300
I heard you quit the team.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:04.940
Yeah.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.910
I mean, the tournament's over.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.180
I wanted to keep playing with everyone,

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.970
but the boys have
a different goal than me now.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.330
A different... goal?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.850
I seriously had a ton of fun, though!

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:28.430
So it's okay. We even won the championship.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:32.650
All right! Time to focus on
entrance exams! Let's do this!

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.010
You got over that quick...

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.970
What school are you applying to?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.890
I'm going for Satogahama.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.140
Then I'll apply there, too.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:44.830
Huh? Um... You might be 
cutting it a little close...

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.110
Really?!

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.190
Tomocchi!

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.320
Okay, okay! I'll help you study.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.700
I'm so glad you got in.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.980
All thanks to you, Tomocchi!

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:15.010
That was impressive!
Think you could've hit that?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.650
Maybe? I think I...

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:20.970
I'm done with all that now.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.940
You know, I used to hate baseball.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:36.770
Because when you first started playing, 
you stopped hanging out with me.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:39.290
I felt like I'd lost my friend.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.740
I-I'm sorry...

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:44.420
But then... when I saw
how much fun you were having,

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.430
I slowly grew to like it.

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:48.950
I was surprised to see
how crazy you were about it.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.750
Tomocchi...

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:53.790
And you still... love baseball, don't you?

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.270
See? You look so happy!

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.010
N-Not really...

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.940
No more lying to your best friend, okay?

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:05.470
Okay...

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:10.190
I... really do love baseball.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.330
Let me join you from now on!

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.010
Huh?

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.570
I'm saying, let's play together!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.780
Come on!

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:22.700
I caught it!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.180
Nice catch!

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:29.030
Thanks... Tomocchi.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.090
So that's what happened.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:37.790
I was surprised when I found out 
Satogahama didn't have a baseball team,

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.680
but I decided I'd start a team
 with Tomocchi's help

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.310
and bring baseball lovers together

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:47.520
so we can all enjoy the
sport I love to the fullest!

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.580
So thank you all for joining me.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.610
It's not as if we're here 
just for you, though.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.270
It's because we want to play!

00:09:57.270 --> 00:10:00.020
Sure. But I wanted you all to know that.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.990
I mean, with two more members,
we can actually field a team!

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:05.710
That's true. We need nine people.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:10.000
Maybe I'll sign up, too.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:11.710
Really?!

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:15.150
I had a lot of fun
in those batting cages, and...

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:18.180
Your tale tugged at my heartstrings.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:22.640
Girls' baseball isn't just bursting
with dreams, but with drama, too!

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:24.850
Super glad to be here.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.230
Super glad to have you!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.410
That means...

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.590
We only need one more!

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.690
I think it's time we worked 
out everyone's positions.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.980
Good idea.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.160
If anyone has a position 
they want to play, speak up.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.640
Mind if I volunteer to play catcher?

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.870
I want to put everything 
I've learned to use.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.020
That seems like a perfect fit for you.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.790
Yeah! You do know a lot about baseball.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:53.840
Sounds great!

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.320
I'll be rooting for you!

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.550
<b>Sports Medicine
and Improving
Your Batting Form</b>

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.300
We'll need to come up with
a pre-game practice regimen.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:09.490
I found the sports section!

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:11.450
This one looks good!

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:13.940
We should find one
that's more for beginners.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:18.780
I can't wait to start
playing in actual games!

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.420
We still need one more member
before we can do that.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:29.810
It'd be great if
Shinonome-san joined us, but...

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:34.000
You're wasting your time if you're
here to ask me to join your team.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.960
I'm aiming at going pro.
I don't have time to mess around.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:38.480
<b>Sports Medicine
and Improving
Your Batting Form</b>

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:44.520
Oh, Shinonome-san.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.470
Did you hear us?

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.920
My answer won't change.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.780
Right. We know it won't.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:56.400
Oh, did you say your club 
team tryout was on Saturday?

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.620
Yes, I did.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.360
Why?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.070
No reason.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:09.490
<i>Keep goofing off with
your friends all you want.</i>

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:14.290
<i>I'm going to go much further.</i>

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:43.360
<b>Takizawa Baseball Club Tryout Site</b>

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.630
Hurrah! Hurrah!

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.920
Shinonome!

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:05.270
Hurrah! Hurrah! Shinonome! 
Hurrah! Hurrah! Shinonome!

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:07.800
What are <i>you</i> doing here?!

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.140
We're cheering you on!

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.290
I never asked you to do that!

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.640
Well, you've gotta cheer on your friends!

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.100
F-Friends?

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:19.060
The baseball association is for 
friends to enjoy baseball together!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.770
You're crazy!

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:23.610
Tryouts will now begin.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.840
Participants, please line up by position.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.990
Go get 'em, Shinonome-san!

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:36.410
The tryouts will be conducted in the form 
of a game against our starters.

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:40.130
You'll each get a go, so when it's
your turn, show us what you can do.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.130
Yes, Coach!

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.180
It's starting!

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:43.840
Yep!

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.720
That guy might be future pro material!

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.510
Um... I should've asked this earlier,

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:58.230
but how is a club team
different from a sandlot team?

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:02.440
The biggest difference is that
they get to play in official games.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:05.730
Some club teams are operated by businesses,

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:08.290
while others, like this one,
are run by volunteers.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:11.590
Many pro players start out on club teams.

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:12.730
Oh...

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:14.870
She's up next!

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:24.870
You can do it, Shinonome-san!

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:27.670
It's all about guts and gumption! Shinonome!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.410
I got it! I got it!

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:57.620
Second!

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.330
Don't worry about it.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.590
You'll get it next time.

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:05.300
My bad.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:15.470
Safe!

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.270
This isn't just some game!

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:22.370
I'm serious about this! You think you can...

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.540
What happened?

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:36.240
The pressure got to her...

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:51.640
If Shinonome-san gets a hit, 
they could take the lead.

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.720
This is a tryout. It doesn't
matter who wins or loses.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.720
Still, at the rate this is going, she's...

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.200
<i>Again?</i>

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:26.170
<i>Am I going to helplessly flame out
without reaching my goal yet again?</i>

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.250
Shinonome-san!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.290
<i>I'm...</i>

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.570
Shinonome-san!

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:32.250
<i>No!</i>

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:36.810
Hurrah! Hurrah! Shinonome!

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:38.810
Go, go, Shinonome!

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.600
You're just getting started, Shinonome!

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.480
Stop it already!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.560
I won't stop!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:44.560
Why not?!

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.810
I don't want you to give up like I did!

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:48.600
Huh?

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:53.280
I already gave up on 
playing baseball my way once,

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:57.330
so seeing you trying so hard 
to take the next step amazes me!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.570
Even if I can't play with you,

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:03.580
I want you to keep playing 
baseball the way you want to!

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.980
So I want to cheer you on!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.170
You can do it!

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:15.720
Hurrah! Hurrah! Shinonome!

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.430
Hurrah! Hurrah! Shinonome!

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:23.600
Hurrah! Hurrah! Shinonome!

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:25.850
Go, go, Shinonome!

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:28.810
Don't lose, don't lose, Shinonome!

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:29.910
You guys...

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:35.340
There may be times when being
cheered on puts you under more pressure.

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:37.990
But when you're feeling
tense or discouraged...

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:44.910
I believe that just having someone 
calling out to you can give you courage.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:48.490
You can do it!

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.900
Next time! There's always next time!

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.610
Don't worry about it!

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:54.330
You can still do this!

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.210
Honestly, just give it a rest.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:01.550
Who said anything about giving up?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.100
<i>I'll decide when this is over.</i>

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.770
<i>And my baseball days won't end here!</i>

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.440
Nice catch!

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:13.650
Yours was good, too.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:14.700
Nice catch!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.320
Let's lock these guys down!

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.610
Yeah!

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.200
Go for it, Shinonome-san!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.740
G-Go for it!

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.180
Take a swing!

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:26.700
It's not over yet!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.240
You almost had it!

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:36.760
You'll get the next one!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.890
Nice running!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.850
That's it!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.480
Way to go, Shinonome-san!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.180
Go!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.490
Okay, let's start individual practice.

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:46.370
Here!

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:56.170
Hey, you guys...

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:59.720
What... kind of practice is this?

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:08.650
You need to lower your hips
in preparation for catching the ball.

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:10.640
R-Right!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:11.790
Also...

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.160
Hold the bat tighter.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:19.310
But don't grip harder than necessary.

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:20.820
O-Okay!

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:25.320
For soft toss hitting, 
aim for the center of the ball.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:28.620
W-Wait... What happened with the tryouts?

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.010
As for the person throwing...

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:37.590
She totally ignored her...

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.510
Tell us how it turned out! 
We're dying to know!

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.820
I failed.

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:12.440
So what? It is what it is.

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:18.740
Don't get the wrong idea. I have no regrets.

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:20.750
In the end, I gave it my all.

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:26.710
<i>I...</i>

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:29.770
<i>I can get stronger.</i>

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.350
Give me the ball.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:41.320
Sure!

00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:00.250
Girls' Baseball Association

00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:00.250
<b>Officially in Action!</b>

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:04.010
<b>Girls' Baseball Association</b>

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:04.460
<b>Officially in Action!</b>

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:04.460
<b>A real hardball baseball team just for girls</b>

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:19.940
<b>Next Time</b>

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:19.940
<b>Our First Game!</b>
